From 1bb4cbdd89c56bb20e648db6cba60d85fc9d3d7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 01:15:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland.drv: Add StatusNotifierItem tray support

Wayland does not have an XEmbed system tray selection, so tray icons hosted
by explorer are not visible when winewayland.drv is the desktop driver.
Publish docked explorer tray icons as StatusNotifierItem objects on the
session bus.

Keep a single D-Bus connection per process and dispatch it from a
Wine-created thread. This lets SNI activation methods queue Wine window
messages without entering win32u from a foreign pthread. The queued callback
then relays button, context-menu, and scroll notifications to the owning
application.

This keeps tray item lifetime in explorer, which already owns Wine tray
hosting across short-lived launcher processes.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
